Format `*.BUILD.bazel` overlays as Starlark.

rules_lint selects a language's files by GitHub Linguist's patterns, and
Linguist knows `BUILD.bazel` but not `foo.BUILD.bazel` -- the name a BUILD file
takes when it is written for an external repository and handed to
`http_archive(build_file = ...)`. So the one class of Starlark file that a
repository writes *about* third-party code is the one the formatter silently
skips, and a check that skips a file class quietly is worse than no check.

The list already carries `*.MODULE.bazel` for the same reason, so this is that
precedent applied to the other half of the convention.

Worth sending upstream. The list is generated by
`format/private/mirror_linguist_languages.sh` from Linguist itself, so the
upstream change is either there or in Linguist's languages.yml -- this patch
only fixes the generated output.

--- a/format/private/format.sh
+++ b/format/private/format.sh
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@
       'SCSS') patterns=('*.scss') ;;
       'Scala') patterns=('*.scala' '*.kojo' '*.sbt' '*.sc') ;;
       'Shell') patterns=('.bash_aliases' '.bash_functions' '.bash_history' '.bash_logout' '.bash_profile' '.bashrc' '.cshrc' '.flaskenv' '.kshrc' '.login' '.profile' '.zlogin' '.zlogout' '.zprofile' '.zshenv' '.zshrc' '9fs' 'PKGBUILD' 'bash_aliases' 'bash_logout' 'bash_profile' 'bashrc' 'cshrc' 'gradlew' 'kshrc' 'login' 'man' 'profile' 'zlogin' 'zlogout' 'zprofile' 'zshenv' 'zshrc' '*.sh' '*.bash' '*.bats' '*.cgi' '*.command' '*.fcgi' '*.ksh' '*.sh.in' '*.tmux' '*.tool' '*.trigger' '*.zsh' '*.zsh-theme') ;;
-      'Starlark') patterns=('BUCK' 'BUILD' 'BUILD.bazel' 'MODULE.bazel' '*.MODULE.bazel' 'Tiltfile' 'WORKSPACE' 'WORKSPACE.bazel' '*.axl' '*.bzl' '*.star') ;;
+      'Starlark') patterns=('BUCK' 'BUILD' 'BUILD.bazel' '*.BUILD.bazel' 'MODULE.bazel' '*.MODULE.bazel' 'Tiltfile' 'WORKSPACE' 'WORKSPACE.bazel' '*.axl' '*.bzl' '*.star') ;;
       'Swift') patterns=('*.swift') ;;
       'TSX') patterns=('*.tsx') ;;
       'TypeScript') patterns=('*.ts' '*.cts' '*.mts') ;;
